  "findings": "Compared full multi-stem form and early spring habit photographs, then current small, medium and large pilots and all 36 seeded variants. The revised coppice grows tapered stools with daughter shoots attached along actual curved stems; leaves follow terminal twig forks. Open irregular outlines and varied stem lean replace spherical crowns. The leaf flush is deliberately fuller than the early-spring photograph, consistent with late spring. Individual serration and catkins are below the selected 25 mm representation. Accepted as a stylized spring hazel coppice source; seed endorsement remains a user decision.",
